  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Context & Request**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the context. The user provided the full file tree and dependencies, plus a detailed request. This includes specifics like a \"Sansera Engineering Logo\" and a \"Hero Background Video.\" The video exemplifies precision manufacturing and robotics, a crucial element for context. My current focus is to decode this data and generate something.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Concepts**\n\nI\'ve been gathering several \"Product Images,\" \"Manufacturing Images,\" and other visuals. I\'m focusing on \"connecting rods,\" \"crankshafts,\" \"robot lines,\" and \"assembly lines\" that were uploaded. Also, a \"Sansera logo image\" and a reference PDF/screenshot is now informing the visual direction. I\'m looking at the header, hero sections, and \"Who We Are\" content to build a concise brief.\n\n\n**Synthesizing Company Narrative**\n\nI\'m now integrating Sansera\'s core values. Sustainability and automation are key, reflecting their commitment to responsible growth. Capabilities like precision forging and machining are becoming clear, and I am incorporating key partners like Hero and Honda. I\'m focusing on their in-house machine building. The \"Let\'s Build the Future Together\" CTA and financial results from the investor kit will shape the desired direction.\n\n\n**Evaluating Asset Integration**\n\nI\'m now assessing the integration of visual assets, specifically the uploaded video. I need to figure out how to incorporate it effectively, considering options like a video element, procedural animation with a canvas, or even visual asset generation. The goal is to align the video with the \"Elegant Dark\" design theme, with its precision engineering aesthetics. I\'m also examining the available tools for asset loading and manipulation within this environment.\n\n\n**Verifying Asset Locations**\n\nI\'ve hit a slight snag, but I\'m making progress. I was initially searching for assets on disk, but I now understand that user-uploaded files are likely in the multimodal context. I\'m verifying this, specifically looking for the \"SANSERA ideas@work\" logo and the provided product and factory images. I\'m re-assessing whether to use SVG, Canvas, or high-resolution assets directly, or if I need to generate or extract them. My focus is still to have an elegant and clean final version.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
