  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Font and Style**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the aesthetic aspects, specifically selecting premium Google Fonts. I\'m leaning toward Inter, Plus Jakarta Sans, Outfit, Space Grotesk, and Syne to achieve a high-tech, precision engineering feel. I am also investigating the implementation of smooth scroll behavior, custom scrollbar styling, and a clean page title: \"Sansera Engineering Limited.\"\n\n\n**Defining Logo and Video**\n\nNow I\'m diving into the specifics of the logo and hero video. I need to authentically reproduce the Sansera logo as an SVG. My plan is to include crisp high-res SVG renderings and glowing active states for both light and dark modes. The hero video will incorporate an interactive loop of robotic manufacturing footage and a 3D canvas simulation. This will also have live telemetry.\n\n\n**Analyzing Visual Assets**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the visual assets, and I need to determine how best to showcase them. My current focus is embedding high-definition visuals, interactive 3D SVGs, canvas elements, and high-res vector representations. I plan to incorporate interactive 3D component viewers with 360-degree rotation, exploded views, and material inspection capabilities. I feel that is key.\n\n\n**Structuring Website Content**\n\nI am now structuring the website content and am focused on the top navigation bar. I\'m planning for a sticky, dynamic glassmorphism effect on scroll. I\'m also including the Sansera logo, along with a \"ideas@work\" badge, a stock ticker, and quick action buttons. I will also incorporate a full mega-menu drawer accessible via a hamburger menu. The hero section is next, and I need to define the exact copy and layout.\n\n\n**Defining Hero Bottom Section**\n\nI\'m now detailing the hero section\'s bottom, with \"40+ Years Heritage | 17+ World-Class Facilities | 10,000+ Skilled Workforce | Top Tier 1 Global Supplier\" as the key elements. The \"Who We Are\" section details the company\'s story, founded in 1981 in Bangalore, India, and its four-decade legacy. It will include a timeline of key milestones and a product segment showcase, which will be interactive.\n\n\n**Detailing 3D Component Views**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in detailing the 3D component views. I\'ve compiled a detailed list of automotive, non-automotive, and aerospace components to showcase, including crankshafts, connecting rods, and actuator components. I\'m planning an interactive tab switcher with 3D/schematic views, hotspot inspection, and data like tensile strength. I\'ve also defined our core pillars: integrated engineering, advanced manufacturing, and automation leadership. Lastly, I will highlight our sustainability efforts.\n\n\n**Defining Sustainability and Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now detailing sustainability efforts with ISO certifications, renewable energy (45MW+), and zero liquid discharge, along with interactive ESG metrics. I\'m also outlining comprehensive capabilities, including design, forging, machining, automation, heat treatment, and quality assurance, alongside their specific features. I\'m focusing on \"Designed, Built, and Optimized In-House\" machine building.\n\n\n**Outlining Strategic Advantages**\n\nI\'m now detailing competitive advantages, specifically in designing and building proprietary CNC machine tools, automated gantry systems, and robotic inspection cells in-house. I will incorporate an interactive \"Machine Builder\" to demonstrate cycle time reduction, cost efficiency, and modular flexibility. I\'m also planning an interactive OEM ecosystem filter, and I need to gather partners: Hero MotoCorp, JCB, Honda, KTM, Volkswagen, Yamaha, Bajaj, Maruti Suzuki, Boeing/Airbus Tier-1, Stellantis, Ducati, and Harley-Davidson. I need a robust investor relations section that will include live stock tracking, results, and financial charts. I will also make an interactive facility section.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Site Layout**\n\nI am now focusing on the website\'s structure and global presence. I\'m detailing the interactive map of our 17+ global facilities, showcasing their specializations, surface areas, and certifications. I\'m also building an interactive RFQ builder, covering industries, components, materials, and volumes. A global office directory and comprehensive footer will be included.\n\n**Elegant Dark Theme**\nI\'m now also exploring an elegant dark theme using deep obsidian/charcoal `#07090e` and `#0b0f19` for the background, with precision metallic borders (`border-white/10`).\n\n\n**Organizing Code Structure**\n\nI\'m now focused on organizing the codebase for optimal readability and maintainability. I\'m defining specific modular files, including types, comprehensive data storage, navbar, hero section, and about section components, to ensure a clean and scalable structure. My current goal is defining types and structures for data management.\n\n\n\n**Defining Core Website Sections**\n\nI\'m now detailing the core website sections, starting with an interactive timeline. I\'ve also defined the `/src/components/ProductSegments.tsx` and its 3D interactive viewer, which will feature exploded views, rotation, and specs. The `/src/components/CapabilitiesSection.tsx` is planned with interactive tabs. I also need to make a in-house CNC deep dive.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 583038607
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
