  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing the Logo Module**\n\nI\'m now focused on building the custom `SanseraLogo` component module, designed as a highly precise SVG vector. It will feature the \"SANSERA\" lettering, bold, clean, italic, and blue, alongside \"ideas@work\" in dark gray, with that distinctive cyan-blue dot on the \"i.\" The design prioritizes responsive scaling and light/dark mode contrast for optimal visual presentation.\n\n\n**Designing the Navbar**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to `src/components/Navbar.tsx`, aiming for an elegant, dark, responsive navbar. It will incorporate a sticky, glassmorphic background, a live NSE stock ticker, quick links, and a prominent Request for Quote button. The design includes a mega-menu drawer and mobile menu for streamlined navigation.\n\n\n**Developing Core Sections**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the core content sections. I\'m building out the \"Contact Our Experts\" section, and an \"Interactive 3D Showroom\" area. I will also incorporate live KPI stat badges for a strong first impression. I\'ve also moved on to `src/components/AboutSection.tsx`, where I\'m crafting a \"Who We Are\" narrative that will be anchored around a timeline of engineering excellence.\n\n\n**Expanding the Capabilities Module**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the `CapabilitiesSection.tsx` module. I am designing six core capabilities with interactive tab selections. Each tab will show real-time specs, equipment details, capacity data, and a live animated diagram. I will create a modal for each component, presenting full technical specs, downloadable CAD datasheets, simulations, and a direct RFQ inquiry link.\nI am also building out an `InHouseMachineBuilding.tsx` module, to spotlight the \"Designed, Built, and Optimized In-House\" advantage, with an interactive cycle time comparison between Sansera\342\200\231s proprietary SPM and traditional machines.\n\n\n**Showcasing Global Partnerships**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `GlobalOEMs.tsx` module, highlighting partnerships with leading global OEMs. I\'m building interactive filters to categorize OEMs by industry (Two-Wheeler, Passenger Car, Commercial, Aerospace) and providing component supply breakdowns. I\'m also including `SustainabilitySection.tsx`, which showcases our commitment to responsible growth, including solar energy, ZLD, and circular scrap recycling. Finally, I\'m building `InvestorRelations.tsx` with a live NSE stock ticker, calculators, and key financial documents. I\'m also integrating an interactive `GlobalFootprint.tsx` map with a facility selector.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 908856335
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
